# .NET & C# Coding Rules

- Target C# 14 / .NET 10.
- Use file-scoped namespaces (`namespace CalendarWidget.Core;`).
- Mark classes `sealed` by default unless explicitly designed for inheritance.
- Mark immutable fields and references `readonly`.
- Use primary constructors where clean and expressive.
- Prefer records for DTOs and value objects.
- Nullable reference types are enabled (`#nullable enable`). Do not suppress with `!` without concrete safety justification.
- Avoid `var` when the underlying type is not obvious from the assignment.
- All public APIs must have XML doc comments (`/// <summary>`).
- Enforce formatting using `dotnet format`.
